    <h2 id="starting-balances">Setting starting balances</h2>
    <p>
      Your money pool balances start at whatever you enter during the <em>Current Balances</em>
      step of onboarding. If you skipped or estimated low, the Debit pool will look wrong by week
      one. Update any pool any time:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>Go to <strong>Settings → Payment Methods → Money Setup</strong>.</li>
      <li>Tap <strong>Debit</strong> and enter your current checking account balance.</li>
      <li>If you carry cash regularly, tap <strong>Cash</strong> and enter what you have on hand.</li>
      <li>If you have money already set aside for savings goals, tap <strong>Savings</strong>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      You don't need to enter your credit card balance unless you want to reflect existing debt in
      the Credit pool. For most people, starting Credit at zero and logging new charges from today
      forward is the right approach.
    </p>
    <div class="doc-tip">
      <strong>Why does the starting balance matter?</strong> Safe to Spend is calculated from your
      budget allocation, not your bank balance. But the Debit pool is a running total of what you
      have in your account based on what you tell BudgetBaby. If it starts at zero, the pool goes
      negative as you log transactions, which is confusing. Set it once and it carries forward
      automatically each period.
    </div>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Money Setup" caption="Tap each pool to set or update its current balance.">
