    <h2 id="budget-periods">Budget periods</h2>
    <p>
      A budget period is a fixed window of time matching your pay frequency. When a period ends,
      BudgetBaby archives it as read-only and opens a new one the next time you launch the app.
      Understanding periods helps you read your history and manage carryforward correctly.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Cash and Debit balances always carry forward.</strong> Whatever your Cash and Debit
        balances are at period end become the starting balances for the next period. This reflects
        real money that stays in your account regardless of pay-period boundaries.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Credit and Savings are managed separately.</strong> Credit owed is tracked per
        period; Savings goal balances are managed through goal contributions and transfers.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Budget surplus can roll over.</strong> If you spend less than your budget, the
        unspent remainder can carry into the next period. You can enable or disable this in
        Settings → Budget Settings.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Bills regenerate each period.</strong> A bill due on the 1st appears in every
        period containing the 1st, you don't recreate bills monthly.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Archived periods are permanent.</strong> The History tab shows every past period
        with all transactions intact. Nothing is deleted when a period closes.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
