    <h2 id="first-week">Your first week</h2>
    <p>
      The first week with BudgetBaby is when you build the habits that decide whether the app stays
      useful. Setup is fast; the habit takes a little longer.
    </p>

    <h3>Days 1 and 2: Set up and calibrate</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Complete onboarding. Make sure each enabled pool has a real Current Balance.</li>
      <li>Add your regular recurring bills with the right priority colors. Rent is red. Streaming
      services are green.</li>
      <li>Log every purchase from today forward, even small ones. Week-one data is what makes Safe
      to Spend trustworthy.</li>
      <li>Create a cloud backup right away: Settings → Backup &amp; Restore → Create Backup. This
      protects the data you're starting to build.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Days 3 through 5: Learn to read Safe to Spend</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Before any discretionary purchase, check Safe to Spend the same way you'd check a bank
      balance.</li>
      <li>Tap the info button next to Safe to Spend to see the full breakdown, period budget,
      spent, bill reserve, savings reserve, days remaining, and the resulting daily rate.</li>
      <li>Mark bills as paid when you pay them. This releases the Bill Reserve immediately and Safe
      to Spend rises to reflect the freed capacity.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Days 6 and 7: Review and adjust</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Open Insights and look at your spending breakdown. Are categories assigned correctly? Are
      any transactions in the wrong payment method? Fix anything that looks off.</li>
      <li>If Safe to Spend seems wrong, check: Is income entered correctly in Budget Settings? Are
      any bills incorrectly showing as unpaid? Are starting balances accurate?</li>
      <li>Adjust settings that don't reflect your reality. The goal is a system you trust enough to
      consult before spending.</li>
    </ul>

